{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/987645-defensive-obfuscate-devotion","id":987645,"title":"Defensive Obfuscate Devotion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-14T23:48:59-07:00","id":987645,"title":"Defensive Obfuscate Devotion","content":"Preface: I'm trying to brain storm a devotion that can use obfuscate in combat with being a huge cost sink.<br /> <br /> Submitted for your reading enjoyment some brain storming<br /> <br /> Page 140 Devotions<br /> <br /> I'm using Wraith's Presence as precedent for what I'm trying to do.<br /> page 149<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Wraith\u2019s Presence<br /> (Obfuscate \u2022\u2022\u2022, Nightmare \u2022)<br /> With this Devotion, the vampire can make herself or<br /> something else vanish from the mind\u2019s eye, but appear<br /> elsewhere. This diversion can distract a pursuer, or make<br /> someone rush after a false lead.<br /> This Devotion costs 2 Experiences to learn.<br /> Cost: 1 Vitae<br /> Dice Pool: Wits + Subterfuge + Obfuscate<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Activate this Devotion when using Cloak of Night. The<br /> vampire projects an exact image of the desired subject in<br /> another place she can see. The image stays mostly still unless<br /> the vampire concentrates on moving it. It\u2019ll make the necessary<br /> motions to appear realistic \u2014 for example, an image of a human<br /> will breathe. The image cannot talk or make noises. The image<br /> vanishes as soon as anyone touches it.<br /> Breaking this effect without touching the phantom uses the<br /> normal Clash of Wills rules (see p. 125).</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> I'm trying to make a replacement effect for Cloak of the Night that will last for a combat. So I don't have to reapply Cloak of the Night if I want it's defensive effect.<br /> <br /> This proposed devotion(found below) would change the combat flow for a cloak of Night user. From a costly. Cast attack Cast attack. With a lot of safety. Into a simple combat buff, with relative safety. With a borrowed mechanic, and a Vitea cost to use it, I don't see this spiraling out of control into chaos. Especially considering that standard Celerity is pretty balanced. This also allows the obf vamp to be a continued presence in a fight if he chooses; be a sneaky get or be shadowy. Options are good.<br /> <br /> Obfuscate has some illusion/mind effects at the higher levels, where as at the lower levels it has ignore/ someone-else's-problem effects. Three being the tipping point. And since this is more geared to a defensive bent, I think it's ok at the level. While Nightmare has illusion effects right off the bat.<br /> <br /> Plays off the themes of fear and hidden threat<br /> <br /> As far as exp cost, It's typically total dots/2 rounded down, plus or minus one depending on how versatile or specific the power is. Considering the power does only one thing and it's defensive I'm thinking about letting it stay at 1 exp<br /> <br /> What I'm looking for is some wide feedback. Where I am missing something, and how this wouldn't work; thematically, mechanically, logically. Has anyone else tried this before, and how did they do it/ What conclusions did they come to?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Through a Glass Darkly<br /> (Obfuscate \u2022\u2022\u2022, Nightmare \u2022)<br /> With this Devotion, the vampire can make herself a more difficult opponent to hit in a fight. She creates a semipermeable illusion around herself masking her location in the mind's eye as slightly ajar from her actual location.<br /> <br /> This Devotion costs 1 Experience to learn<br /> Cost: 1 Vitae<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> <br /> Instead of applying Cloak of Night on a subject Add Obfuscate dots to target's defense rating for the scene as like Celerity. Celerity cancels this effect. Does not work against animals or those without a mind.<br /> <br /> Stylized as Static/ Warping/ After Images/ licking Shadows/ Blood Dripping/ Torn Ribbons whatever the vampire decides would be appropriate. Haunts often use a more pronounced and exaggerated version of their clan flaw.<br /> <br /> The method of learning and homing this Devotion is rather alarmingly self destructive. The vampire must somehow use her own darkness to evade taking hits. She must do this continually until such a point where her beast starts instinctively playing illusionary effects onto her attackers. This may be accomplished over many training sessions, but those looking for a shortcut sometimes intentionally provoke the beast with it's banes. Theses sessions have shown quite effective provided that the kindred lives through the harrowing ordeal. Afterwards this cost efficient Devotion can really help a Haunt or Shadow out, when blood is thin in the night to night struggle.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T01:55:10-07:00","id":987677,"title":"","content":"Sorry for this post, problem with pc and I can't to delete it now. Read the fallowing post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 10-15-2016, 04:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T01:56:29-07:00","id":987678,"title":"","content":"What about something like that:<br /> <br /> Shadow Hit:<br /> (Obfuscate 3, Celerity 1)<br /> <br /> The vampire, invisible, hits his unaware enemy disappearing in a blink of an eye.<br /> <br /> Cost: 1 or 2 vitae<br /> Dice pool: none<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> <br /> Spending with a reflexive action the cost of the devotion, the vampire can disappear from the perception everytime he want. He can attack and become invisible again before the target could react.<br /> <br /> (this implies a -5 penality dice to any attack roll against the vampire, plus his defense, and the possibility to make another surprise attack in the next turn)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T06:16:47-07:00","id":987717,"title":"","content":"Mrr.....<br /> <br /> The Familiar Stranger already does the first one. Touch, and boom. Instantly change how anyone sees the subject. Trying to recreate a highler level power at a cheaper / lower level leaves me cold and doubtful. Furthermore, Devotions build upon existing abilities, not on ability levels. It doesn't make sense to have illusion powers from an ability that doesn't use illusions, even if you think its the right &quot;power level.&quot; I recommend just getting Obfuscate 4 and a cheap devotion with Celerity to make it reflexive. <br /> <br /> Through a Looking Glass feels like it is trying to replace Celerity's main effect without having to buy Celerity. You even have that it can't be used with Celerity, which is very odd considering that Celerity's defense boost is passive - active uses of Celerity are initiative changes and speed boosts. So, if you possess even one dot of Celerity, this devotion can never be used. It makes little sense from a design point of view. I also have to question the justification of inflicting - Obfuscate operates on the principle of <i>hiding auras</i>. This is inflicting your predator's aura on other's minds in an pseudo-offensive manner - you should have just gone with &quot;the vampire is blurry and hard to aim at.&quot; Much simpler and thematically appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T10:33:31-07:00","id":987821,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7079_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7079\" data-vbnamecard=\"7079\">Marcus</a> <br /> <br /> Thank you for taking the time to read and give feedback <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That's a nice devotion idea, but that's not exactly what I'm aiming for. That is the Cast Attack, Cast Attack, flow that I'm trying to avoid. Every turn you'd be bleeding extra vitea. and effectively making yourself untargetable for the entire fight, as long as you have the vitea for it. That's great but not what I'm trying to go for.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2102_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2102\" data-vbnamecard=\"2102\">MCN</a> <br /> <br /> Likewise. Thank you for taking the time to read and give feedback <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Wraith's Presence is taken directly from Blood and Smoke page 149. Yes, I wanted to avoid Celerity+Ofsuc Def tracks. A possible +10 def feels way too power. Breaks the +5 chains the system is based on. Plus Celerity has all its interrupting and innovative shenanigans. This only borrows it's mechanical passive with a cost.<br /> <br /> The proposed goes with the burry effect. semipermeable illusion. Cloak of Night allows you to disappear from sight. That is total concealment/ illusion. I wanted to make something half way that could persist through combat. Like half concealment illusion.The proposed is layering half of Cloak of Night's effect with a Nightmare illusionare effect. and spending vitae to make it lasting. Creating like a mirror image/ continual after image effect. Something Like a Blur or Mirror Image Spell in DnD.<br /> <br /> Like Half the character is visually there and the other half is out of phase, and an nightmarish illusion is taking it's place. It's not supernatural celerity quickness, it's mind games. I'm borrowing a mechanic from another power which people agree is balanced to represent that effect. While at the same time trying to avoid creating a total imbalance of stacking powers. Yes Celerity is superior than the proposed, that is by design. It is not meant to completely replace Celerity, but offer an alternative.<br /> <br /> Familiar stranger doesn't give you any mechanical bonuses in combat, but I do see what you're saying.<br /> <br /> True, Devotions build upon existing abilities. But I've always read Devotions are kind of in an open area of design space as long as their thematically aligned. Look at The Wish page148. I don't believe any vanilla discipline can grant another discipline dots. And Shatter the Illusion page 146. Auspex revealing + Vigor Strength.<br /> <br /> A Obfuscate4 Celerity1 devotion would do what? Allow quick changing of profiles in real time. Their perceptions of the character emotionally would change rapidly, but the character would still be physically in the same place to them. I'm saying I don't need their emotional perceptions to the vamp changing, the user needs their opponent's Hand Eye coordination to be off tilt, while at the same time still rocking their own attacks.<br /> <br /> And I believe there is grounds for a devotion that purely mind fck's the person into distraction using only obfuscate.<br /> <br /> But I would take the stance that CoN more than allows for the you're not there effect the proposed is trying to emulate. Level three obfuscate the vamp vanishing in front of people's eyes. Much like Wraith's Presence, but played closer to hand/body. and I would further take the stance that a little bit of nightmare can make characters on edge enough to allow some mindfcking. Reasons I wouldn't put it lower, is because, Face in Crowd allows for ignore effects, until violence kicks off, and therefore not good enough. Touch of Shadow allows you to impart some of your obf effects onto other targets, again not good enough. But CoN hits that sweet spot of unconditional vanishing, which can persist.<br /> <br /> And a obf4cele1 devotion would be what Marcus proposed<br /> <br /> I appreciate the feedback, thou I believe the celerity may have been a point of miscommunication, and I should have cited the book better","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T10:58:41-07:00","id":987837,"title":"","content":"Since you don't want it to be stackable with Celerity, what about making it involve Celerity in its prerequisites and modify the way Celerity works. Like, what if you combined Face in the Crowd's &quot;ignore me!&quot; function with Celerity's defense boosting? Something like...<br /> <br /> Motion Blur<br /> (Celerity 1, Obfuscate 1)<br /> By using Celerity to enhance her reflexes and Obfuscate to obscure her movements, the vampire becomes almost impossible to hit.<br /> Cost: 1 Vitae<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Duration: Scene.<br /> While this Devotion is active, the vampire does not add Celerity to her Defense. Instead, all attackers that she can perceive subtract the higher of her Celerity or Obfuscate from their dice pools to hit her.<br /> This Devotion costs 1 Experience to learn.<br /> <br /> So, you might get a slight boost by using the higher of Celerity or Obfuscate, and by applying a penalty directly to attackers instead of a bonus to defense you don't get diminishing returns with multiple attackers, and it still penalizes them if you Dodge, make an All-Out Attack, or sacrifice your Defense for a Fighting Style Maneuver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T14:59:24-07:00","id":987950,"title":"","content":"Interesting and fair Idea Char. My concern there is if Face in the Crowd ignore me effect be reasonable strong enough to be applicable in a fight. As it is stated to cancel upon violence. Thematically it works with Obfuscate 's Hidden and unseen themes, and it works with Celerity's Movement, Speed and Defense themes. Seems reasonable scaling wise. And the idea of take dice from attacks rather than adding to def is a cool work around. Thanks for the idea<br /> <br /> I still really like the SPFX from the original proposal. Instead of vanishing from sight from the first sign of trouble. Rolling out a wave of like illusionare Barb wire. Which is the domain of nightmare. Hmm maybe I should rethink and rework my idea. Save that for later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}